                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e6db17b9-a6f4-3a99-bd86-db3daf6bb106",
                        "entry_id": "06b613a8-1560-3455-8883-8585f664e2a4",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Heimlich maneuver."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "6d24ec5c-a533-4aef-b3c0-0299e4169e97",
                                "sense_id": "e6db17b9-a6f4-3a99-bd86-db3daf6bb106",
                                "text": "They choke to death on water. […] Four Heimlichs take ten seconds to perform and anyone can do them. The Red Cross adopted the Heimlich."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "470a0889-af58-4aae-abc0-7740445f0771",
                                "sense_id": "e6db17b9-a6f4-3a99-bd86-db3daf6bb106",
                                "text": "Having never done a Heimlich on a dog myself, I have no way to know for sure.\nTHE HEIMLICH MANEUVER\nThe Heimlich for a Small Dog\n1. Lay the dog on her side on a flat, hard surface.[…]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3e879e67-e494-4308-98f3-1765867dac03",
                                "sense_id": "e6db17b9-a6f4-3a99-bd86-db3daf6bb106",
                                "text": "- Demonstrate finger sweeps\n- Explain the use of the Heimlich on infants\n- Explain the use of the Heimlich on children\n- Explain the use of the Heimlich on pregnant patients[…]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f12bb3ab-7f15-4db3-897b-2ed2b90bcfd8",
                                "sense_id": "e6db17b9-a6f4-3a99-bd86-db3daf6bb106",
                                "text": "He's choking, I think I yelled, help me turn him on his side. And I thumped him on the back and pushed up into his belly but we couldn't get our arms [around...] I would have stopped him, whacked him on the back, tried several Heimlichs on [him...]"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
